294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 260 0 R
/E (A person's voice is more than just a way to communicate. It is a part of their identity and helps others recognize them. People with conditions such as ALS, Parkinson's disease, stroke, laryngectomy, or dysarthria slowly lose their ability to speak. As their voice changes, it becomes difficult for them to communicate and express themselves. Most existing voice cloning and Text-to-Speech \(TTS\) systems need clear and healthy voice recordings to create a good voice model. They also cannot adjust when a person's voice keeps changing because of the disease. As a result, the generated speech may not sound like the person's original voice. EchoGenesis is an AI-based voice preservation system that can learn from short or partially affected voice recordings. It preserves the person's unique voice and generates clear, natural speech, allowing them to continue communicating in a voice that sounds like their own even as their condition progresses.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
